            <ArticleTitle>Evaluation of quality of life in indian children with bronchial asthma using a disease-specific and locally appropriate questionnaire.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>554-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To evaluate quality of life (QOL) in Indian children with bronchial asthma.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">A disease-specific, locally appropriate QOL questionnaire was administered in asthmatic children and compared with FEV1, FVC, PEFR and asthma symptom score, on three occasions.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">QOL score had strong negative correlation with symptom score and weaker positive correlation with pulmonary function tests.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Disease-specific QOL score correlates inversely with symptom score in children with bronchial asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
